From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:23:36 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: enable USB on the FRITZ!Box 7560

The box has one USB host port, on the SoC's usb1; usb0 is not bonded
out. Enable the controller and its PHY and give the PHY the VBUS supply
it needs.

Port power is software controlled through gpio0 line 6, active high.
That polarity is one of the few AVM annotations worth trusting, because
two independent things in the vendor tree state it: the board file
marks the line GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH (AVM 4.9 arch/mips/boot/dts/lantiq/avm/
grx350_common.dtsi, gpio_avm_usb_power_enable) and the shim that drives
it uses gpiod_set_value(), which honours the flag. Contrast the LED
annotations in the same file, which are wrong precisely because that
shim never read them.

The vendor does not model this as a regulator at all. It patches
drivers/usb/host/xhci.c to resolve the line through an AVM-private
alias, fails module init when the alias is missing, forces it low in
xhci_hcd_init(), and raises it from a delayed work item 100 ms after
xhci_run_finished(). A regulator-fixed consumed by the PHY through
vbus-supply needs no patches to shared code and raises VBUS in
phy .power_on, i.e. before the controller starts rather than after --
a stricter ordering, and the one the USB spec asks for. It is stricter
in a way that has not been tested on this hardware yet, so if a device
fails to enumerate, that 100 ms post-start delay is the first vendor
behaviour to reproduce.

The Phase-14 placeholder in the pin map goes away with this: gpio0 6 is
now claimed, by the regulator, the same way gpio0 8, 9 and 16 are
claimed by the PCIe root complexes.

No pinmux. The pad comes up as a plain GPIO, which is all the regulator
needs, and there is nothing to mux it to: the vendor deletes every USB
pinctrl node it declares, and pinctrl-equilibrium has no USB function
or group at all.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
index 060ca4b593c8..cf26ea178c63 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dtsi
@@ -262,3 +262,23 @@ &pcie2 {
 	intel,outbound-swap = <0>;
 	reset-gpios = <&gpio0 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 };
+
+/ {
+	usb_vbus: regulator-usb-vbus {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "usb_vbus";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		gpio = <&gpio0 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+	};
+};
+
+&usb1_phy {
+	status = "okay";
+	vbus-supply = <&usb_vbus>;
+};
+
+&usb1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
